One bitter winter, an ancient terror known as the White Void descended from the peaks. It was a suffocating, dense blizzard that swallowed the pale sunlight and deadened all sound, leaving Kaelen lost on a crumbling cliffside. He played his flute in a desperate plea for aid, but the heavy snow smothered the melody entirely.

Unwilling to let the frost consume the mortal he favored, Zephyr hurled his glowing quartz core against the sheer canyon wall. The impact shattered his physical form, embedding millions of iridescent fragments into the stone. When Kaelen played his flute a final time, the quartz shards caught the dying vibration. Zephyr’s fractured spirit amplified the note, blasting it outward to shatter the White Void and guide Kaelen home.

Zephyr never reformed. Now, whenever travelers shout into the canyons, his scattered shards throw their voices back.
